# Settings of this install. "docker compose run --rm setup init" writes .env
# from its arguments and keeps every line it is not given.
# .env is gitignored. Never commit it: it can hold the Wyze password.
#
# How to type a value by hand: KEY=value, with no space before or after "=".
# If the value has a space, a $, a # or a double quote, put the whole value
# in single quotes: WYZE_PASSWORD='my pass#word$1'. A value with a single
# quote ' cannot go in single quotes; change that value. Type straight
# quotes, not curly ones. init, sync and doctor check each line and say
# which key Docker would read in another way (they never print the value).

# --- Where and when -----------------------------------------------------------

# Time zone, as an IANA name such as Europe/Berlin or America/New_York.
# The first init needs it (--tz). doctor flags UTC.
TZ=
# The folder for recordings, clips and snapshots. A relative path is relative
# to this folder. Use a disk with room. doctor measures the size of a day of
# recordings for each camera and says when the disk is full at that rate.
MEDIA_DIR=./media
# Days of continuous recording to keep. sync puts this number in the Frigate
# config; the exporter uses it too.
RECORD_DAYS=7
# Days to keep each event clip (media/exports). Empty: for ever. The least is
# 3, so that a clip is never cut again while its event is still in the list.
CLIP_KEEP_DAYS=

# --- Ports on this computer -----------------------------------------------------

# The app, on 127.0.0.1 only.
APP_PORT=5010
# The admin site: Frigate's own UI with no login, and the Wyze bridge's UI,
# on 127.0.0.1 only. Open http://127.0.0.1:5011 on this computer.
ADMIN_PORT=5011
# Frigate's own UI with Frigate's login (HTTPS), and WebRTC live view.
FRIGATE_HTTPS_PORT=8971
WEBRTC_PORT=8555
# The address that the two ports above listen on. 127.0.0.1: this computer
# only. 0.0.0.0: every network of this computer (other devices at home can
# then reach Frigate's login page).
FRIGATE_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1

# --- Remote view ----------------------------------------------------------------

# The host name that your remote proxy sends, for example the name that
# "tailscale serve" gives this computer (name.tailnet-name.ts.net). Empty:
# only this computer can open the app. doctor checks that the app accepts it.
APP_HOST=
# The same for the admin site, if you publish it. Empty: not published.
ADMIN_HOST=
# Extra WebRTC addresses of this computer, comma-separated, for example
# 192.168.1.20:8555. sync puts them in the Frigate config.
WEBRTC_CANDIDATES=
# The contact in each push message (a mailto: or https: address). Empty:
# https://<APP_HOST>.
VAPID_SUBJECT=

# --- Cameras --------------------------------------------------------------------

# "wyze" runs the Wyze bridge. init sets it when WYZE_EMAIL is set.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=
# Wyze account. API_ID and API_KEY come from
# https://developer-api-console.wyze.com/#/apikey/view
WYZE_EMAIL=
WYZE_PASSWORD=
API_ID=
API_KEY=
# Only for a Wyze account with two-step login: the TOTP secret (the key that
# your authenticator app was set up with). Empty for an account without it.
WYZE_TOTP_KEY=
# Cameras inside the home, comma-separated Frigate camera names. A bark alert
# is sent only for these cameras, and only when nobody is seen on them.
INDOOR_CAMERAS=
# Cameras that sync must not add, comma-separated. "setup remove <camera>"
# adds the name here.
SKIP_CAMERAS=
# The detector: openvino (x86-64) or cpu (arm64, such as a Mac with Apple
# silicon). Empty: init and sync pick it from the processor of this computer.
FRIGATE_DETECTOR=
# Frigate's shared memory. sync raises it when the cameras need more (and
# says that a restart is needed). Empty: 256mb.
FRIGATE_SHM_SIZE=

# --- The pet day ----------------------------------------------------------------

# The pet day is off unless both PET_NAME and PET_CAMERA are set.
PET_NAME=
# The Frigate camera name of the room where the pet spends the day.
PET_CAMERA=
# dog or cat.
PET_LABEL=dog
# male or female: the story uses he or she.
PET_SEX=male

# --- Summaries from a local vision model (optional) -----------------------------

# The Ollama address, for example http://host.docker.internal:11434 for
# Ollama on this computer. Empty: no summaries, and the pet day story is a
# plain template. The model is qwen2.5vl:7b ("ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b").
OLLAMA_URL=
# "nvidia": summaries wait while another program holds the NVIDIA GPU (the
# cam-helper container then needs a GPU reservation, which you add in a
# docker-compose.override.yml). Empty: no wait.
GPU_GATE=
